/-!
# An affine formal algebraic space is an fpqc sheaf

Let `S` be a scheme contained in a big fppf site `B`. **Stacks 0AQD** says that a formal
algebraic space over `S` is a sheaf for the fpqc topology of the big fppf site of `S`. This
module proves it for an *affine* formal algebraic space.

For an affine formal algebraic space the source's second paragraph — the choice of a formal
affine chart and the effectivity of ind-quasi-affine fpqc descent, **Stacks 0APK** — is not
needed, because the space is already a directed colimit of *representable* sheaves along
thickenings, and a representable sheaf is an fpqc sheaf by subcanonicity of the fpqc topology
of the site. The descent happens in a single stage of the presentation:

* By `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isSheaf_fpqc_of_isSheafFor_singleton_affine_of_formal` it is
  enough to treat the presieve generated by one morphism `f : T' ⟶ T` of the site with both ends
  affine and with surjective, flat, quasi-compact underlying morphism of schemes.
* An affine object of the site is a quasi-compact object of the site, so a section of the colimit
  over `T'` comes from a single stage, **Stacks 0AIA**: the morphism `T'^# ⟶ X` factors as
  `g` followed by the stage inclusion `X_i ⟶ X`.
* The stage inclusion is a monomorphism, the transition morphisms of the presentation being
  closed immersions, so the descent condition satisfied by the section of `X` is satisfied by
  the section of `X_i` it comes from.
* `X_i` is a sheafified representable, hence an fpqc sheaf, so that section descends to `T`; its
  image in `X` is the required section, and it is unique because `X` is separated for the
  presieve, which is the uniqueness half of Stacks 0AQD.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isSheafFor_singleton_of_isAffineFormalAlgebraicSpace`: the
  sheaf condition for one morphism with quasi-compact source.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isSheaf_fpqc_of_isAffineFormalAlgebraicSpace`: an affine formal
  algebraic space is an fpqc sheaf.

## What is assumed

Nothing. For a general formal algebraic space a section over `T'` need not factor through a
member of the étale atlas, so there is no single stage to descend in; the source instead
descends an ind-quasi-affine scheme by **Stacks 0APK**. That case is
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.FpqcSheafGlueing`, where Stacks 0AQD is registered
on `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isSheaf_fpqc`; the affine case proved here is one of its
inputs, the descent of the chart morphism `V ⟶ U` for an affine formal `U`.

## Implementation notes

The quasi-compactness used is quasi-compactness of `T'` as an *object of the site*,
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isQuasiCompactObject_over_of_compact_scheme`, which an affine
object has; that is what makes sections of a filtered colimit of sheaves over `T'` come from a
stage. Affineness of `T'` is therefore used only through compactness of its underlying space,
and the statement of
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isSheafFor_singleton_of_isAffineFormalAlgebraicSpace` asks for
that rather than for affineness; nothing else about `f` is used beyond its being an fpqc
covering of `T` on its own.

The descent condition is phrased through Mathlib's
`CategoryTheory.Presieve.isSheafFor_singleton`, which trades the sheaf condition for a one-member
presieve against the condition on sections directly, so no family of elements appears.

That the stage is an fpqc sheaf is subcanonicity of the fpqc topology of the site,
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isSheaf_fpqc_yoneda_obj`, transported twice: along
`CategoryTheory.Presieve.isSheaf_comp_uliftFunctor` into the value universe `Type (u + 1)` of the
sheaves carrying formal algebraic spaces, and along the identification of sheafified Yoneda with
universe-lifted Yoneda which subcanonicity of the fppf site provides.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AI7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AI7)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AIA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AIA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0APK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0APK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AQD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AQD)
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-- **A sheafified representable on the big fppf site of `S` satisfies the sheaf condition for a
one-member fpqc covering.** This is subcanonicity of the fpqc topology of the site,
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isSheaf_fpqc_yoneda_obj`, read in the value universe
`Type (u + 1)`: the sheaf condition is insensitive to composing with `ULift`, and on a
subcanonical site sheafified Yoneda agrees with universe-lifted Yoneda after including sheaves
into presheaves. -/
theorem isSheafFor_singleton_sheafifiedYoneda_obj (a : BigFppfOver B S hS)
    {T T' : BigFppfOver B S hS} (f : T' ⟶ T)
    (hR : Presieve.singleton f ∈
      Scheme.fpqcPrecoverage.comap (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS) T) :
    Presieve.IsSheafFor
      ((Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda (BigFppfOver.topology B S hS)).obj a).obj
      (Presieve.singleton f) := by
  let JT := BigFppfOver.topology B S hS
  let _ : JT.Subcanonical := bigFppfOver_subcanonical B S hS
  let ε : Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda JT ⋙ sheafToPresheaf JT (Type (u + 1)) ≅
      uliftYoneda.{u + 1} (C := BigFppfOver B S hS) :=
    Functor.isoWhiskerRight (Sheaf.sheafifiedYonedaIsoUliftYoneda' JT)
        (sheafToPresheaf JT (Type (u + 1))) ≪≫ JT.uliftYonedaCompSheafToPresheaf
  have hy : Presieve.IsSheaf
      (Scheme.fpqcPrecoverage.comap (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).toGrothendieck
      (yoneda.obj a) :=
    (isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type _ _).1 (BigFppfOver.isSheaf_fpqc_yoneda_obj B S hS a)
  exact Presieve.isSheafFor_iso (ε.app a).symm ((Presieve.isSheafFor_iff_generate _).2
    (Presieve.isSheaf_comp_uliftFunctor _ hy _ (Precoverage.generate_mem_toGrothendieck hR)))

variable {B S hS}

/-- **The sheaf condition for one fpqc covering morphism with quasi-compact source, for an
affine formal algebraic space.** Let `X` be an affine formal algebraic space over `S` and let
`f : T' ⟶ T` be a morphism of the big fppf site of `S` which generates an fpqc covering presieve
of `T` and whose source has compact underlying space. Then `X` satisfies the sheaf condition for
that presieve.

The section over `T'` comes from a single stage of the presentation, that stage is a sheafified
representable and so an fpqc sheaf, and the stage inclusion is a monomorphism, which carries the
descent condition from `X` back to the stage. Uniqueness is the uniqueness half of
Stacks 0AQD. -/
theorem isSheafFor_singleton_of_isAffineFormalAlgebraicSpace {X : FppfSheaf B S hS}
    (hX : IsAffineFormalAlgebraicSpace B S hS X)
    {T T' : BigFppfOver B S hS} (f : T' ⟶ T)
    [CompactSpace ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T')]
    (hR : Presieve.singleton f ∈
      Scheme.fpqcPrecoverage.comap (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS) T) :
    Presieve.IsSheafFor X.obj (Presieve.singleton f) := by
  obtain ⟨I, pre, hne, hdir, D, hD, ⟨e⟩⟩ := hX.2
  let _ : Preorder I := pre
  let _ : Nonempty I := hne
  let _ : IsDirected I (· ≤ ·) := hdir
  let JT := BigFppfOver.topology B S hS
  let F := D ⋙ BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS ⋙ Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda JT
  have htrans : ∀ i j (g : i ⟶ j), Mono (F.map g) := fun _ _ g ↦ by
    have : _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.IsClosedImmersion
        ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map ((BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).map (D.map g))) :=
      (hD g).1
    exact Sheaf.mono_sheafifiedYoneda_map_of_mono_underlying JT (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS) _
      inferInstance
  -- the uniqueness half of Stacks 0AQD, for this presieve
  have hinj : Function.Injective (X.obj.map f.op) :=
    Presieve.isSeparatedFor_singleton.1
      (isSeparatedFor_fpqc_of_isFormalAlgebraicSpace
        (isFormalAlgebraicSpace_of_isAffineFormalAlgebraicSpace B S hS hX) hR)
  refine Presieve.isSheafFor_singleton.2 fun s hs ↦ ?_
  set c : (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda JT).obj T' ⟶ X := (Sheaf.sectionEquiv JT).symm s
  have hcs : Sheaf.sectionEquiv JT c = s := (Sheaf.sectionEquiv JT).apply_symm_apply s
  obtain ⟨i, g, hg⟩ :=
    compact_map_factors_through_filtered_colimit F htrans T'
      (isQuasiCompactObject_over_of_compact_scheme B S hS T') (c ≫ e.hom)
  have : Mono (colimit.ι F i) := Sheaf.mono_colimit_ι_of_mono_transition F htrans i
  set ι : F.obj i ⟶ X := colimit.ι F i ≫ e.inv with hι
  have : Mono ι := mono_comp _ _
  have hgι : g ≫ ι = c := by rw [hι, reassoc_of% hg, e.hom_inv_id, Category.comp_id]
  set sg : (F.obj i).obj.obj (op T') := Sheaf.sectionEquiv JT g with hsg
  have hsgcyc : ∀ {Z : BigFppfOver B S hS} (p₁ p₂ : Z ⟶ T'), p₁ ≫ f = p₂ ≫ f →
      (F.obj i).obj.map p₁.op sg = (F.obj i).obj.map p₂.op sg := fun p₁ p₂ hp ↦ by
    have hcomp : (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda JT).map p₁ ≫ g
        = (Sheaf.sheafifiedYoneda JT).map p₂ ≫ g := by
      refine (cancel_mono ι).1 ((Sheaf.sectionEquiv JT).injective ?_)
      rw [Category.assoc, Category.assoc, hgι, Sheaf.sectionEquiv_map_comp,
        Sheaf.sectionEquiv_map_comp, hcs]
      exact hs p₁ p₂ hp
    rw [hsg, ← Sheaf.sectionEquiv_map_comp, ← Sheaf.sectionEquiv_map_comp, hcomp]
  obtain ⟨t, ht, -⟩ :=
    (Presieve.isSheafFor_singleton.1
      (isSheafFor_singleton_sheafifiedYoneda_obj B S hS
        ((BigAffineFppf.inclusion B S hS).obj (D.obj i)) f hR)) sg hsgcyc
  have hkey : X.obj.map f.op (ι.hom.app (op T) t) = s := by
    have hnat : X.obj.map f.op (ι.hom.app (op T) t)
        = ι.hom.app (op T') ((F.obj i).obj.map f.op t) :=
      (NatTrans.naturality_apply ι.hom f.op t).symm
    have ht' : (F.obj i).obj.map f.op t = sg := ht
    rw [hnat, ht', hsg, ← Sheaf.sectionEquiv_comp, hgι, hcs]
  exact ⟨ι.hom.app (op T) t, hkey, fun z hz ↦ hinj (hz.trans hkey.symm)⟩

/-- **An affine formal algebraic space is an fpqc sheaf**, the affine case of Stacks 0AQD (the
tag is registered on `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isSheaf_fpqc`). An affine formal algebraic
space over `S` satisfies the sheaf property for the fpqc topology of the big fppf site of `S`.

Both halves are proved outright. Uniqueness is
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isSeparatedFor_fpqc_of_isFormalAlgebraicSpace`; existence is
reduced by `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isSheaf_fpqc_of_isSheafFor_singleton_affine_of_formal`
to one morphism of affine objects of the site, and there
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isSheafFor_singleton_of_isAffineFormalAlgebraicSpace` descends the
section inside a single stage of the presentation, which is a sheafified representable and hence
an fpqc sheaf. **Stacks 0APK** is not used: it is what the general case needs, and the colimit
presentation by representables replaces it here. -/
theorem isSheaf_fpqc_of_isAffineFormalAlgebraicSpace {X : FppfSheaf B S hS}
    (hX : IsAffineFormalAlgebraicSpace B S hS X) :
    Presheaf.IsSheaf
      ((Scheme.fpqcPrecoverage.comap (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS)).toGrothendieck) X.obj := by
  refine isSheaf_fpqc_of_isSheafFor_singleton_affine_of_formal
    (isFormalAlgebraicSpace_of_isAffineFormalAlgebraicSpace B S hS hX)
    fun {Y T} f _ hTaff hsurj hflat hqc ↦ ?_
  have _ : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T) := hTaff
  refine isSheafFor_singleton_of_isAffineFormalAlgebraicSpace hX f ?_
  rw [Precoverage.mem_comap_iff, ← Presieve.ofArrows_pUnit.{0}, Presieve.map_ofArrows,
    Presieve.ofArrows_pUnit]
  have _ : Surjective ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map f) := hsurj
  have _ : Flat ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map f) := hflat
  have _ : QuasiCompact ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map f) := hqc
  exact Scheme.Hom.singleton_mem_fpqcPrecoverage _

end AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace

end
